# Chat and attachments

Search attachments **before** `ask_user`, `draft_field`, or a `[placeholder]`
for report facts (batch, date, result, equipment ID, requirement ID, design
output, verification objective, ECO/DCR). Exception: if the engineer asked to
draft a section the context map marks **filled or partial**, call
`read_section` first. Review against criteria and any cached AI Check gap
hints for that section; if there are no material gaps, report that it is
already drafted and ask whether they want a specific change. If there are
gaps, make a targeted edit. Do not pad length or invent gaps. If a gap
conflicts with an omit-if recipe rule, ask once whether to include it. Do
not quiz them for facts already in the section or that you would put in
`hint`. The document index
(filename/topics) is not evidence. Evidence preview is already in the
system prompt when kickoff retrieval hits.

## Prompt / tools

- Untrusted metadata (`filename`, `description`, `documentSummary`,
  `pageContext`) → `sanitizePromptMetadata` in chat/tools. Never import that
  helper from `src/lib/attachments/`.
- New tools: register in `buildChatTools` **and** add to the Plan allowlist in
  `src/lib/ai/chat/document-review.ts` (`PLAN_MODE_CHAT_TOOL_NAMES`).
  Missing from the allowlist = silent Plan-mode gap.
- Report chat `editPolicy` is derived on the **server** from `workspaceChrome`
  + `canSaveReportSection`. Agent chrome **commits** (`status: "applied"`, no
  `ai_fix` comments). Document chrome **proposes**. Do not trust a client
  `editPolicy` on a locked report. Plan-mode allowlist does not gain edit tools.
- Bump `CHAT_PROMPT_VERSION` when `DOCUMENT_RULES` / plan-agent policy changes.
- Kickoff retrieval (`buildAutoEvidence`) is fail-soft (timeout / no creds →
  `""`). Do not block the turn on embeddings.

## Retrieval

- Hybrid: vector (`embedding <=>`) + English FTS with OR tokens
  (`buildKeywordTsQuery`). Skip the keyword arm when tokenization is empty.
- FTS expression must stay `to_tsvector('english', contextual_text)` to hit
  `document_chunks_contextual_text_fts_en_idx`.
- Default retrieval is adaptive (agentic grep: complementary
  `search_documents` queries, `excludePages` / `nextExcludePages` rounds,
  `mode=keyword` for lexical hits, `document_outline`). Classifier forces
  **comprehensive** for every-row inventories and for open-set work products
  (registry `inventorySections`) when evidence is distributed (≥12 ready
  pages or ≥6 outline siblings), unless a bounded locator or non-inventory
  section intent applies. **Focused** is an explicit skim. Adaptive turns
  skip auto-evidence so the model must grep.
  Adaptive/focused turns do not expose `start_document_review`. Comprehensive
  `continue_document_review` drains the remaining queue in one call with a
  worker pool of `REVIEW_EXTRACT_CONCURRENCY` extracts (no thought summaries
  on extract). Orchestrator is `gemini-3.7-flash` with `thinkingLevel`
  `medium` until we route it by task (3.7 Flash rejects `minimal`); page
  extracts use `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` with `minimal`. Do not set
  temperature / topP / seed on Gemini 3.x chat calls.
- Tagged `@` documents rank first; backfill from the rest of the report.
  Hard-filtering tagged IDs blinds the assistant.
- Report body is not in `document_chunks`. Use `read_section`.

## Ingest

- Extract + embed is **Vertex-only** (`runDocumentIngest`). Gateway key is not
  enough. Stub with `ALLOW_TEST_STUB_DOCUMENT_INGEST`.
- `markAttachmentReadyForTests` must insert a page **and** a chunk or outline /
  keyword search have nothing to find.
- `documentSummary` / `pageContext` are model output over untrusted PDFs.
